# Roshan Rozgar — all of this is OPTIONAL.
#
# With an empty .env the backend still runs end to end: an embedded Postgres
# (PGlite) is created under .data/pglite, and every AI endpoint answers from a
# deterministic offline stub labelled `provider: "stub"` in its response meta.
# That label is what the UI surfaces and what the README discloses — per the
# brief, mocked functionality must never be presented as working.
#
# Blank `KEY=` lines are treated as unset, so you can copy this file as-is.
#
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# Then verify what you have configured:   npm run check:integrations

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Database — leave blank to use embedded PGlite (no account, no credentials)
#
# Supabase: Project -> Connect -> "Session pooler" string. Use the POOLER
# string, NOT "Direct connection": the direct host (db.<ref>.supabase.co) is
# IPv6-only and fails on most home networks. Replace [YOUR-PASSWORD] and
# URL-encode any special characters in it. Looks like:
#   postgresql://postgres.<ref>:<password>@aws-0-<region>.pooler.supabase.com:5432/postgres
#
# After setting it:  npm run db:migrate && npm run seed -- --keep
# (plain `npm run seed` TRUNCATES the app tables first; --keep does nothing if
# the database already has workers.)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# DATABASE_URL=
# PGLITE_DATA_DIR=./.data/pglite

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Anthropic — reasoning, extraction, classification, translation, summaries
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-...
# ANTHROPIC_MODEL=claude-sonnet-5-5
# ANTHROPIC_MODEL_HEAVY=claude-opus-5-5

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# OpenAI — Whisper for Urdu speech-to-text (fallback behind ElevenLabs Scribe)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# OPENAI_API_KEY=sk-...
# OPENAI_STT_MODEL=whisper-1

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# ElevenLabs — Urdu speech-to-text (Scribe, leads the transcribe chain) and
# text-to-speech for reading prompts aloud (GET|POST /api/ai/speak).
# Keys: elevenlabs.io -> Developers -> API keys.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# ELEVENLABS_API_KEY=
# ELEVENLABS_STT_MODEL=scribe_v1
# ELEVENLABS_TTS_MODEL=eleven_v3
# Free plan: premade voices only (library voices return 402). Default is "Alice".
# ELEVENLABS_VOICE_ID=Xb7hH8MSUJpSbSDYk0k2

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Gemini — reserved. The key is read but no Gemini provider is implemented.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# GEMINI_API_KEY=...

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Supabase Storage — voice notes and work photos.
# Leave blank to store uploads on local disk under .data/uploads, served by
# GET /api/upload/[name]. Local storage is fine for the demo; set these if
# uploads must survive a redeploy on Vercel (its filesystem is ephemeral, so a
# deployed demo DOES need them).
#
# Project -> Settings -> API: the project URL and the secret / service_role key.
# That key is server-only: never expose it to the browser or commit it.
# The bucket is created automatically (public) on first upload.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Bare project URL only, no path (not the ".../rest/v1/" address).
# SUPABASE_URL=https://<ref>.supabase.co
# SUPABASE_SERVICE_KEY=
# SUPABASE_BUCKET=roshan-media

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Search tuning (defaults shown; see PROJECT.md §3.4 for the ranking formula)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# SEARCH_DEFAULT_RADIUS_KM=8
# SEARCH_MAX_RESULTS=20
